    {
      "id": "claim_9489ddd3ab184022bac73328a51ac43e",
      "statement": "The argv-secret gate (scripts/check-no-argv-secrets.mjs) fails the build if any in-scope tracked file passes a credential-named --env/-e argument to the Maestro test runner, because that re-serialises the secret onto argv where ps and /proc expose it on a shared CI host; the sanctioned path is scripts/maestro-run.sh, which forwards secrets through the MAESTRO_-prefixed environment channel.",
      "evidence": [
